\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces  Figure summarizing the interaction of the different factors; speed of climatic shift, width of species dispersal kernel and landscape configuration, and their role for changed population density. The size and color of the circles correspond to the change in global population density between start of the climatic shift and end of the simulation. The panels in the lower row is describing landscapes with different distributions of habitat patches, and the species disperse from left to right in the landscapes.\relax }}{29}}
